Thanks to Robert Schueler, Paul Sand Jie Gao and Nikola Milutinovic.

Quoting from one of the replies:

"If your apache is in a path with any softlink in it, you might hit a
known bug: apache finds the library twice and has everything defined
twice."

and in fact that was the case, since the directory I download stuff into is 
on a different machine to the one that it gets installed into.  With NFS, 
it's easy to forget things like that....

Moving the tar into a directory on the same machine as the installation 
target directory allowed the make and install to run smoothly.  I did this 
on two machines, one with gcc-3.3.2 and the other with just the default C 
compiler and it was fine on both (although slower using gcc).

Cheers
Derek
