Hi managers.

As usual answers and suggestions arrives at an amazing rate :-)

summary of problem:
My problem was that i wanted my unix machines to use an internal server as
mail gateway, but no matter what i tried
they kept on trying to go outside the house to get the adress of my
mailserver.



The following were so kind to guide me in the right direction:

Kalle Henk
Thomas Sjolshagen
Phil Baldwin
Udo de Boer

I tried to fiddle with mailsetup and bindsetup to no help, then Phil Baldwin
suggested that it was propably=20
resolv.conf and scv.conf who were the reasons to my problems, he was right.

In svc.conf i took all bind,yp of from all the lines
and then i renamed resolv.conf to something else....

I also checked my sendmail.cf and found no DR line so i inserted one and
corrected th DW line to reflect my host file


Now my 2 unix servers are perfectly isolated from any external nameservers,
and i have the desired functionality..




