On Tue, 24 Feb 2004 12:26 pm, you wrote:

Thanks to Jan Mark Holzer from HP Long Term Planning and Support Group for his 
quick response.

In Jans reply he pointed me into the direction of it being the hotswapd
 daemon not responding.  So what I did was, that I looked to see if the 
hotswapd was running on the system which it wasn't so, I then checked 
the /etc/inittab file and then found that it was not listed in 
the /etc/inittab but it was in my other 5.1a machines so I added the nessary 
entries in to the inittab and then typed init q and now all is well.

The /etc/inittab entry that was missing 

hsd:Ss:sysinit:/sbin/hotswapd < /dev/console > /dev/console 2>&1


